        "original_id": "295df527-8580-5bdf-a848-ca60dcac6bd7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sila Region, Dar Sila, Chad, Ouaddaï Region, Libya, Sudan, Central African Republic, Cameroon, Nigeria, Niger, Markounda\n- Organizations: departments of Sila, Djourf Al Ahmar\n\nFacts:\n- Sila, also called Dar Sila, is a region of Chad that was created in 2008 from the departments of Sila and Djourf Al Ahmar, which had previously been part of Ouaddaï Region.\n- Chad is bordered by Libya to the north, Sudan to the east, the Central African Republic to the south, Cameroon and Nigeria to the southwest, and Niger to the west.\n- Markounda is a sub-prefecture that borders Chad.",
